Release a Metal context's free buffers once another context is current on its thread (Minato, patch 0032).

Why: the buffer manager and its free list are a context's own (ContextMtl::mBufferManager). Ren'Py's display reset
during a pause makes a new context on its render thread (pygame_sdl2's recreate_gl_context), loads its whole scene in
it and, once SDL makes the old context current again, never makes the new one current again nor destroys it. Its free
list, filled by the load up to patch 0029's 64 MiB, stayed with it: about 48 MiB more per return that raced in the
Simulator (where Metal's buffers are shared memory), never shrinking. Upstream's collection runs only while the
context is current (120 switches, 5000 commits or 64 MiB more allocated).
Now onUnMakeCurrent notes the context for its thread. When another context is made current on that thread, the noted
one is current nowhere: the buffers the GPU is done with move to its free list and the free list goes down to
kMaxIdleFreeBytes (1 MiB), the largest first, as patch 0029 trims. Made current again first (an app or wrapper that
lets its context go at each frame's end), it keeps its free list: no buffer is made again per frame. A context made
current on any thread, or destroyed, leaves the notes. Buffers the GPU still uses stay in use.
Test: graphics/tests/angle_context_trim.mm (D, sharing C's objects, fills its free list past 32 MiB with 8 MiB
buffers; C made current: at most 1 MiB; D current again draws and clears; D let go and made current again keeps at
least 32 MiB; no context, then C: at most 1 MiB).
Upstream: could go upstream (a context current nowhere keeps no free buffers; cheap at a context switch).
Remove: when upstream frees an idle context's free list or the race's context goes away.
